      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "RAY COOKE AUCTIONEERS are delighted to present this charming bungalow located in a quite cul de sac and highly sought-after pocket of Palmerstown, No. 50 Oakcourt Park.\n\nOakcourt Park is a mature and highly sought-after residential development, renowned for its peaceful surroundings, excellent community atmosphere and superb convenience. Ideally positioned in the heart of Palmerstown, residents enjoy an abundance of local amenities including shops, cafés, schools, sports clubs and picturesque parklands. The Phoenix Park, Liffey Valley Shopping Centre and Chapelizod Village are all within easy reach, while the area is exceptionally well serviced by numerous bus routes and offers quick access to the N4, M50 and Dublin City Centre, making it an ideal location for commuters and families alike.\n\nThe bright and well-proportioned accommodation comprises an entrance porch, generous living room, fully fitted kitchen, an exceptionally large double bedroom (formerly three bedrooms), and a large family bathroom. To the rear, the property boasts a substantial concrete-built workshop, providing superb additional storage, workshop space or excellent potential for a variety of uses. Further benefits include side access, beautifully maintained front and rear gardens, and off-street parking to the front.\n\nOriginally designed as a three-bedroom home, No. 50 has been thoughtfully reconfigured to create an exceptionally spacious one-bedroom bungalow, offering versatile accommodation that could easily suit a variety of buyers. The property has been lovingly maintained over the years and is presented in good clean condition throughout, while also offering excellent potential for the new owner to reconfigure the layout back to its original two-bedroom format, subject to their own requirements.\n\nComing to the market vacant with no onward chain, this is an excellent opportunity for first-time buyers, those looking to downsize, or investors seeking a home with fantastic potential in one of Dublin 20's most desirable locations. Early viewing is highly recommended—contact RAY COOKE AUCTIONEERS today for further information or to arrange a viewing.\n\nFeatures\n\n•Originally 3-bedroom (currently configured as a spacious 1-bedroom)/1 bathroom bungalow\n•BER E1\n•C. 55sqm of internal floorspace\n•Vacant with no onward chain\n•Large concrete-built workshop to the rear\n•Side access\n•Well-maintained front and rear gardens\n•Off-street parking\n•Gas fired central heating\n•Presented in good clean condition throughout\n•Potential to restore original 3-bedroom layout\n•Mature and highly sought-after residential development\n•Excellent transport links including N4, M50 and regular bus routes\n•Close to Phoenix Park, Liffey Valley Shopping Centre, schools and local amenities\n•Ideal for first-time buyers, downsizers and investors\n•Early viewing highly advised\n"
      },
      {
